.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂r}=2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta }=-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bae007ee4068299a4b4b005747985ad13bb9cb305ddf87d91a526afdb610a0a1"} {"question" "q-95130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta "] ["math" "r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )"] ["math" "r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operat