tion $f(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y+2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2z)r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-94770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bae007ee4068299a4b4b005747985ad13bb9cb305ddf87d91a526afdb610a0a1"} {"question" "q-94770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-94770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2rz{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-94770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xyz,$ find $\\frac{∂u}{∂z},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $u(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂u}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂z}+\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂z}+\\frac{∂u}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂u}{∂z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂z}=2{x}^{2}z+xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =2{r}^{2}z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}(2z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bae007ee4068299a4b4b005747985ad13bb9cb305ddf87d91a526afdb610a0a1"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta "] ["math" "2{r}^{2}(z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +{r}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta "] ["math" "{r}^{2}(2z\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )"] ["math" "{r}^{2}(2z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{r}^{2}(2z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $v(x,y,z)=2y-xz,$ find $\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $v(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂v}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂v}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂v}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂v}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $v$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂x}=-z,\\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =-z, \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta } & =-(-z)r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(2)r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bae007ee4068299a4b4b005747985ad13bb9cb305ddf87d91a526afdb610a0a1"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +z\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +2r{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta "] ["math" "z{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +2r{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070474/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7f9877dfa86a81e0f4c430cd615198432b893c2557401c42e9afcea0b48635d"} {"question" "q-95172" "field" "selection" "attribute"